        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT18-088#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT18-088 (Nov. 1, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "You may choose 1 card with a combination of having the [Hybrid] trait and a different name from your trash and place it under this Tamer.  For each of your other Tamers, you add 2 to the maximum number of cards this effect may place under this Tamer.  For example, if you have 1 Tamer other than this Tamer, you can choose up to 3 cards with the [Hybrid] trait and different names from your trash and place them under this Tamer.",
        "question": "What does this card's [Start of Your Main Phase] effect do, exactly?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, it can't attack. A new attack declaration can't be made during an attack.  In such cases, even if you activate this card's [End of Your Turn] inherited effect when you already have an attacking digimon, a new attack can't be performed using a Digimon with this card in its digivolution cards.",
        "question": "My Digimon is attacking using an effect at the end of my turn.  Can I use this card's [End of Your Turn] inherited effect to attack a player using a Digimon with this card in its digivolution cards?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
